---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow">Private by default · Android first</div>
      <h1>Decisions,<br /><em>with evidence.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">Turn rough conversations into decisions you can verify, with the source context still in view.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-dark" href="/support">Get support <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note"><span class="signal"></span> Your source stays on your device by default.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-band" aria-label="How Quorivell works">
    <div class="shell proof-grid">
      <div><strong>01</strong><span>Capture</span><p>Start with the conversation as it happened.</p></div>
      <div><strong>02</strong><span>Review</span><p>Check each candidate against its evidence.</p></div>
      <div><strong>03</strong><span>Follow up</span><p>Keep open commitments visible and clear.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell principles">
    <div class="section-label">The Quorivell principle</div>
    <div>
      <h2>A record should show<br />where it came from.</h2>
      <p>Quorivell is built for the moment after a conversation, when certainty is useful but invention is not. Decisions and commitments remain reviewable, with owners, due dates, and unknowns kept explicit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
